  "difficulty_reason": "The proof designs a state-dependent coupling of infinite rank configurations under simultaneous bin-count and cumulative-count inequalities. Its four-case rank selector uses a rejection probability and a conditional replacement variable, and must preserve the exact reproduction-law marginal and the induction order even with infinite configurations. These local constructions then control conditional insertion probabilities and produce the freezing zero-one law for a process with long memory, beyond ordinary doctoral probability qualifiers; ordinary Borel-Cantelli is only the final named prerequisite.",
